1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Would you hang a giant ham upstairs to avoid a luxury price?

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,200
Vance thought twelve thousand dollars for Spanish ham was outrageous.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,800
Instead of buying expensive slices, he imagined making one himself.

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:14,400
And somehow, his ordinary attic became part of that plan.

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:18,000
First, he ignored the glamorous gourmet shop displays entirely.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,600
He headed to the local market with a very different budget.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,200
The enormous pork leg he carried home looked almost unreal.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,800
But Vance knew buying it was just the beginning.

9
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,400
He weighed the massive cut, already imagining the final result.

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,000
Soon the kitchen counter looked more like an unusual experiment.

11
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,600
The mountain of salt alone made the whole project look absurd.

12
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:43,200
Still, his grocery receipt was nothing like the boutique price.

13
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:46,800
Then a bright red wooden chest appeared in the backyard.

14
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,400
Neighbors probably had questions, but Vance wasn't giving explanations.

15
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,000
Days passed, and the yard slowly changed with the seasons.

16
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,600
After three long weeks, he finally opened the strange chest.

17
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:01,200
What emerged looked surprisingly different from the meat he started with.

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,800
Vance and his friend could barely lift the enormous leg.

19
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,400
But the strangest part of his experiment was still ahead.

20
00:01:08,400 --> 00:01:12,000
He carried that giant ham upstairs into his attic.

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,600
The empty room suddenly had a very unusual new resident.

22
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:19,200
Even Vance had to laugh at his bizarre home setup.

23
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,800
He hoped this space could resemble an old European curing cellar.

24
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:26,400
But months of waiting would test his patience more than anything.

25
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:30,000
A giant piece of meat hanging upstairs looked risky to outsiders.

26
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,600
And a homemade setup is no guarantee that food stays safe.

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:37,200
Still, Vance kept returning to check on his unusual project.

28
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:40,800
The hanging ham gradually took on an almost cake-like white coating.

29
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,400
After more waiting, the moment of truth finally arrived.

30
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:48,000
Vance inspected the ham with the focus of a nervous contestant.

31
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,600
He seemed convinced the enormous gamble had finally worked.

32
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:55,200
So he carried his prize downstairs for the big reveal.

33
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:58,800
The giant leg took center stage on its wooden stand.

34
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:02,400
Almost two months of waiting had led to this moment.

35
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:06,000
The first exposed slice showed a surprisingly deep red color.

36
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,600
It looked remarkably similar to the ham behind gourmet counters.

37
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,200
Vance shaved off thin ribbons as everyone watched closely.

38
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:16,800
Then he finally tasted the result of his long experiment.

39
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:20,400
His reaction suggested he loved the rich, salty flavor.

40
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,000
A little cheese and a crunchy cracker completed his tasting plate.

41
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,500
Then came the final question: how much had he spent?

42
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,000
Vance counted about three hundred fifty dollars for the project.

43
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,500
Against that boutique price tag, the difference looked enormous.

44
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,991
But would you trust a homemade attic ham? That's the debate.
